---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Notice"
  description="How Sibanye Engineering Solutions uses and retains information submitted through its project enquiry form."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Privacy notice"
    intro="Last updated: 28 October 2026"
  />

  <article class="container-x max-w-3xl py-12 sm:py-16">
    <div class="space-y-10 text-base leading-relaxed text-body">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink-950">Who we are</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Sibanye Engineering Solutions (SES) handles information submitted through this website's
          project enquiry form. For privacy questions or requests, email
          <a class="font-medium text-accent-700 underline" href="mailto:corporate@sibanyeengineering.com">
            corporate@sibanyeengineering.com
          </a>.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink-950">Information we collect and why</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          The form asks for your name, email address and project details. You may also provide your
          organisation, phone number and sector of interest. For a valid submitted enquiry, the
          endpoint includes your IP address in the email sent to SES. A SHA-256 hash of the IP
          address is also used in the separate rate-limit file to prevent repeat submissions. We
          use these details to review and respond to your enquiry, manage any resulting engagement,
          and operate and protect the form.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink-950">Service providers</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Email hosting is provided by Real Image. Real Image may process enquiry emails to host
          the SES mailbox and deliver messages. The website hosting provider may also process
          information submitted through the form to operate the site. Enquiry details are sent to
          corporate@sibanyeengineering.com.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink-950">How long we keep information</h2>
        <ul class="mt-3 list-disc space-y-3 pl-6">
          <li>Enquiry emails: 24 months after the last meaningful contact.</li>
          <li>Unsuccessful or abandoned enquiries: 12 months after the last contact.</li>
          <li>
            Enquiries that become client engagements: relevant correspondence is transferred to
            the client record and kept for 7 years after the engagement ends where justified by
            contractual, legal or business requirements.
          </li>
          <li>Mail delivery and error logs: 90 days.</li>
          <li>
            Security and rate-limiting logs: 30 days, unless an incident requires longer retention.
            The separate rate-limit file stores a hashed IP key and removes entries after one hour.
          </li>
          <li>Backups containing enquiry emails: 90 days, after which older backups are securely overwritten or deleted.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink-950">Your questions and requests</h2>
        <p class="mt-3">
          Contact SES at
          <a class="font-medium text-accent-700 underline" href="mailto:corporate@sibanyeengineering.com">
            corporate@sibanyeengineering.com
          </a>
          with questions or requests about your enquiry information, including a request to access,
          correct or delete it. Requests will be handled in accordance with applicable requirements.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
